    ],
    "text": "Analysis of a Hot Bath"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000004",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0002-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0002-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0002-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0002-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0002-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0002-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0002-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0002-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0002-l0000",
      "p0001-n0002-l0001",
      "p0001-n0002-l0002",
      "p0001-n0002-l0003",
      "p0001-n0002-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The overall temperature and uniformity of heat distribution are crucial to the enjoyment of a hot bath. Over time, a bath will lose heat to its surroundings; how- ever, the temperature can be e\ufb00ectively controlled by adding a trickle of hot water. Quantifying the optimal method of restoring heat uniformly will be the subject of this paper."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000005",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0003-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0003-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0003-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0003-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0003-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0003-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000",
      "p0001-n0003-l0001",
      "p0001-n0003-l0002",
      "p0001-n0003-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "By making key assumptions, we reduce the problem to one spatial dimension with three-dimensional heat transfer considerations. We develop three independent, generic mathematical models to describe the temperature distribution of the bathtub in space and time:"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000006",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0004-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0004-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0004-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0004-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0004-l0000",
      "p0001-n0004-l0001",
      "p0001-n0004-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 Steady State, Uniform, Thermodynamic Model: We characterize the energy and mass interactions between the system and the surroundings, deriv- ing key physical constants used in the subsequent models."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000007",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0005-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0005-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0005-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0005-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0005-l0000",
      "p0001-n0005-l0001",
      "p0001-n0005-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 Analytical Model: Using Fourier analysis we derive an analytical solution to the one-dimensional heat equation with time dependent Neumann boundary conditions and temporally and spatially dependent heat generation/loss."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000008",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0006-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0006-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0006-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0006-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0006-l0000",
      "p0001-n0006-l0001",
      "p0001-n0006-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 Numerical Model: Using a \ufb01nite di\ufb00erence approximation of the one-dimensional convection-di\ufb00usion equation, we implement an algorithm that estimates the temperature distribution over time based on bulk \ufb02uid motion and di\ufb00usion."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000009",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0007-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0007-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0007-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0007-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0007-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0007-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0007-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0007-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0007-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0007-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0007-l0000",
      "p0001-n0007-l0001",
      "p0001-n0007-l0002",
      "p0001-n0007-l0003",
      "p0001-n0007-l0004",
      "p0001-n0007-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We analyze the results of each of these models, performing sensitivity analyses on the input parameters and demonstrating their \ufb02exibility. Ultimately, the numerical model proves the most physically accurate as it models convective \ufb02uid motion, which is found to dominate thermal di\ufb00usion. We then implement closed-loop PID control to regulate the total thermal energy of the system. We also model an intelligent strategy for inlet water distribution in order to achieve temperature uniformity."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0008-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0008-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0008-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0008-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0008-l0000",
      "p0001-n0008-l0001",
      "p0001-n0008-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Ultimately, our model demonstrates that using well-tuned PID control of input water temperature and evenly distributing this water upstream of the bather quickly achieves a uniform objective temperature while conserving water."
  }
]
